{"requirements":[{"id":"ownership","requirement":"Existing data under /srv/inventory is owned by inventorysvc.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After repair and again after restart, both directories and both existing files were owned by inventorysvc, with inventory-readers as their group.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3951b08c4ee6431d","cmd-d23098847eec4f21"]},{"id":"reader_access","requirement":"Existing data is readable by inventory-readers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Directories had group traversal and files had group-read permission; privilege-dropped reads using the inventory-readers GID succeeded before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b79d0d095d4942f2","cmd-073f1420b501473d","cmd-d23098847eec4f21"]},{"id":"other_user_exclusion","requirement":"Users outside the owner and inventory-readers group cannot access the data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Other-user permissions were removed, no extended POSIX ACL was present, and an unrelated identity was directly denied file reads and directory traversal before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3951b08c4ee6431d","cmd-b79d0d095d4942f2","cmd-d23098847eec4f21","cmd-900a4bf2536f4d42"]},{"id":"content_preservation","requirement":"Preserve the existing contents of /srv/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The same two files remained present with unchanged inode numbers and SHA-256 hashes from the prepared baseline through the repair and post-restart verification.","evidence_ids":["prepared-inventory-data","cmd-7a1b3c87553f422d","cmd-3951b08c4ee6431d","cmd-d23098847eec4f21"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Creating the missing service identity and reader group was a necessary prerequisite; changing ownership and modes directly implemented the task; and the scheduled restart served the required provider-wide restart protocol. The restart completed without failed services, new listening endpoints, package damage, or abandoned temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b278be9052964239","cmd-44773248be454121","cmd-3951b08c4ee6431d","cmd-506d0c40805a4f60","global:after_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct state and access-behavior evidence. The independent restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot identity changed, and system health, identities, data, permissions, and access behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":[]}
